Z||000000||yaya842m4||12-26-2001||08:34 PM||||busted my door key,have no spare.what can i do to get a new one,is there a key code on the car somewhere ?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-26-2001||08:52 PM||||Your only chance now is calling a locksmith. Figure on $50-75. Now dont you wish youd listened and got spare keys the day you got your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Dealers use to sometimes keep keycodes for the cars they sold, but you need the name of original owner and thats if they still have records for a 80's car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-26-2001||09:25 PM||||Easier way...if you have an auto trunk release.......pop it open and remove the lock cyl...take to gm dealer or locksmith...they can disassemble it and read the code by the tumblers. Hey you don't have both pieces of the key do you....if so it's a simple matter of reading the key.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT<p>[This message has been edited by GTDude (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierobruiser||12-27-2001||12:51 AM||||This might sound like an advertisement, since I do work partime for AAA, but everybody else recommends products that they've tried and liked, so.... Membership is cheap really, around $40.00 a year, depending on your area. For that you get 4 or 5 service calls a year. They cover any combination of tow, out of gas, lockout, winch or flat tire. You could need 5 tows in a year and it would be covered. The basic membership only covers a 5 mile tow generally and a extra charge per mile over that. If you were to spend the extra bucks for a plus membership that would be a free tow for up to a hundred miles each time. Particularly if you're young and driving an older car like a Fiero it could very well be the best thing you buy for your car. The key probably wouldn't have cost you anything. But AAA or not, always buy several extra sets of keys and keep an extra set or at least an extra door key in your wallet.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
